#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch's algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritma Deutsch"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves the parity problem for the special case that $n = 1$.\n"
"In the context of quantum computing this problem is sometimes referred to as *Deutsch's problem*, and we'll follow that nomenclature in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch menyelesaikan masalah pariti untuk kes khas di mana $n = 1$.\n"
"Dalam konteks pengkomputeran kuantum, masalah ini kadangkala dirujuk sebagai *masalah Deutsch*, dan kita akan menggunakan tatanomenklatur itu dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, the input is represented by a function $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ from one bit to one bit.\n"
"There are four such functions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk lebih tepat, input diwakili oleh fungsi $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ dari satu bit ke satu bit.\n"
"Terdapat empat fungsi sedemikian:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first and last of these functions are *constant* and the middle two are *balanced*, meaning that the two possible output values for the function occur the same number of times as we range over the inputs.\n"
"Deutsch's problem is to determine which of these two categories the input function belongs to: constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi pertama dan terakhir adalah *malar* manakala dua yang di tengah adalah *seimbang*, bermakna dua nilai output yang mungkin bagi fungsi tersebut muncul dengan bilangan yang sama apabila kita mengambil semua input.\n"
"Masalah Deutsch adalah untuk menentukan kategori mana fungsi input tersebut tergolong: malar atau seimbang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch's problem\">\n"
"Input:  a function $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Deutsch\">\n"
"Input:  fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ jika $f$ adalah malar, $1$ jika $f$ adalah seimbang\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we view the input function $f$ in Deutsch's problem as representing random access to a string, we're thinking about a two-bit string: $f(0)f(1)$.\n"
msgstr "Jika kita melihat fungsi input $f$ dalam masalah Deutsch sebagai mewakili capaian rawak kepada rentetan, kita sedang memikirkan tentang rentetan dua bit: $f(0)f(1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When viewed in this way, Deutsch's problem is to compute the parity (or, equivalently, the exclusive-OR) of the two bits.\n"
msgstr "Apabila dilihat dengan cara ini, masalah Deutsch adalah untuk mengira pariti (atau, secara setara, XOR eksklusif) dua bit tersebut.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every classical query algorithm that correctly solves this problem must query both bits: $f(0)$ and $f(1)$.\n"
"If we learn that $f(1) = 1$, for instance, the answer could still be $0$ or $1$, depending on whether $f(0) = 1$ or $f(0) = 0$, respectively.\n"
"Every other case is similar; knowing just one of two bits doesn't provide any information at all about their parity.\n"
"So, the Boolean circuit described in the previous section is the best we can do in terms of the number of queries required to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap algoritma pertanyaan klasik yang menyelesaikan masalah ini dengan betul mesti bertanya kedua-dua bit: $f(0)$ dan $f(1).$\n"
"Jika kita mengetahui bahawa $f(1) = 1,$ sebagai contoh, jawapannya masih boleh $0$ atau $1,$ bergantung pada sama ada $f(0) = 1$ atau $f(0) = 0,$ masing-masing.\n"
"Setiap kes lain adalah serupa; mengetahui hanya satu daripada dua bit tidak memberikan sebarang maklumat tentang pariti mereka.\n"
"Jadi, litar Boolean yang diterangkan dalam bahagian sebelumnya adalah yang terbaik yang boleh kita lakukan dari segi bilangan pertanyaan yang diperlukan untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit description {#quantum-circuit-description}"
msgstr "Penerangan litar kuantum {#quantum-circuit-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves Deutsch's problem using a single query, therefore providing a quantifiable advantage of quantum over classical computations.\n"
"This may be a modest advantage — one query as opposed to two — but we have to start somewhere.\n"
"Scientific advances sometimes have seemingly humble origins.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch menyelesaikan masalah Deutsch menggunakan satu pertanyaan sahaja, dengan itu memberikan kelebihan yang boleh diukur bagi kuantum berbanding pengiraan klasik.\n"
"Ini mungkin kelebihan yang sederhana — satu pertanyaan berbanding dua — tetapi kita perlu bermula dari suatu tempat.\n"
"Kemajuan saintifik kadangkala mempunyai asal-usul yang kelihatan rendah hati.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit that describes Deutsch's algorithm:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah litar kuantum yang menerangkan algoritma Deutsch:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Algoritma Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To analyze Deutsch's algorithm, we will trace through the action of the circuit above and identify the states of the qubits at the times suggested by this figure:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menganalisis algoritma Deutsch, kita akan meneliti tindakan litar di atas dan mengenal pasti keadaan qubit pada masa-masa yang dicadangkan oleh rajah ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![States during Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Keadaan semasa algoritma Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state is $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, and the two Hadamard operations on the left-hand side of the circuit transform this state to\n"
msgstr "Keadaan awal adalah $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, dan dua operasi Hadamard di sebelah kiri litar mengubah keadaan ini kepada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(As always, we're following Qiskit's qubit ordering convention, which puts the top qubit to the right and the bottom qubit to the left.) It may feel unintuitive to write this product state partly distributed (leaving the states of qubit 1 factored out), but this will make our later expressions more compact.\n"
msgstr "(Seperti biasa, kita mengikuti konvensyen susunan qubit Qiskit, yang meletakkan qubit atas di sebelah kanan dan qubit bawah di sebelah kiri.) Mungkin terasa tidak intuitif untuk menulis keadaan produk ini sebahagiannya dalam bentuk teragih (meninggalkan keadaan qubit 1 dalam bentuk faktor), tetapi ini akan menjadikan ungkapan kita kemudian lebih ringkas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"According to the definition of the $U_f$ gate, the value of the function $f$ for the classical state of the top/rightmost qubit is XORed onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, which transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, gerbang $U_f$ dilaksanakan.\n"
"Mengikut definisi gerbang $U_f,$ nilai fungsi $f$ untuk keadaan klasik qubit atas/paling kanan di-XOR ke atas qubit bawah/paling kiri, yang mengubah $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ kepada keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can simplify this expression by observing that the formula\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh memudahkan ungkapan ini dengan memerhatikan bahawa formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"works for both possible values $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"More explicitly, the two cases are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"berfungsi untuk kedua-dua nilai yang mungkin $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Secara lebih eksplisit, dua kes tersebut adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we can alternatively express $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ like this:\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, kita boleh menyatakan $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ secara alternatif seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Something interesting just happened!\n"
"Although the action of the $U_f$ gate on standard basis states leaves the top/rightmost qubit alone and XORs the function value onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, here we see that the state of the top/rightmost qubit has changed (in general) while the state of the bottom/leftmost qubit remains the same — specifically being in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state before and after the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"This phenomenon is known as the *phase kickback*, and we will have more to say about it shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sesuatu yang menarik baru berlaku!\n"
"Walaupun tindakan gerbang $U_f$ pada keadaan asas standard membiarkan qubit atas/paling kanan tidak berubah dan meng-XOR nilai fungsi ke atas qubit bawah/paling kiri, di sini kita melihat bahawa keadaan qubit atas/paling kanan telah berubah (secara umumnya) manakala keadaan qubit bawah/paling kiri kekal sama — khususnya berada dalam keadaan $\\vert - \\rangle$ sebelum dan selepas gerbang $U_f$ dilaksanakan.\n"
"Fenomena ini dikenali sebagai *tendangan fasa*, dan kita akan membincangkannya dengan lebih lanjut tidak lama lagi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With one final simplification, which is to pull the factor of $(-1)^{f(0)}$ outside of the sum, we obtain this expression of the state $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Dengan satu pemudahan terakhir, iaitu mengeluarkan faktor $(-1)^{f(0)}$ ke luar jumlah, kita memperoleh ungkapan keadaan $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{jika $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{jika $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that in this expression, we have $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ in the exponent of $-1$ as opposed to $f(1) - f(0)$, which is what we might expect from a purely algebraic viewpoint, but we obtain the same result either way.\n"
"This is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa dalam ungkapan ini, kita mempunyai $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ dalam eksponen $-1$ berbanding $f(1) - f(0)$, yang mungkin kita jangkakan dari sudut pandang aljabar semata-mata, tetapi kita mendapat hasil yang sama dalam kedua-dua cara.\n"
"Ini kerana nilai $(-1)^k$ untuk sebarang integer $k$ hanya bergantung pada sama ada $k$ adalah genap atau ganjil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the final Hadamard gate to the top qubit leaves us with the state\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan gerbang Hadamard terakhir pada qubit atas meninggalkan kita dengan keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{jika $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{jika $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which leads to the correct outcome with probability $1$ when the right/topmost qubit is measured.\n"
msgstr "yang membawa kepada hasil yang betul dengan kebarangkalian $1$ apabila qubit kanan/paling atas diukur.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Further remarks on the phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"
msgstr "Catatan lanjut tentang tendangan fasa {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, let's look at the analysis above from a slightly different angle that may shed some light on the phase kickback phenomenon.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum meneruskan, mari kita lihat analisis di atas dari sudut yang sedikit berbeza yang mungkin dapat menjelaskan fenomena tendangan fasa.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, notice that the following formula works for all choices of bits $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, perhatikan bahawa formula berikut berfungsi untuk semua pilihan bit $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be verified by checking it for the two possible values $c = 0$ and $c = 1$:\n"
msgstr "Ini boleh disahkan dengan menyemaknya untuk dua nilai $c = 0$ dan $c = 1$ yang mungkin:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using this formula, we see that\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan formula ini, kita melihat bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every choice of bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Because this formula is true for $b=0$ and $b=1$, we see by linearity that\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk setiap pilihan bit $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Kerana formula ini benar untuk $b=0$ dan $b=1$, kita melihat melalui kelinearan bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all qubit state vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, and therefore\n"
msgstr "untuk semua vektor keadaan qubit $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, dan oleh itu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key that makes this work is that $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the vector $\\vert - \\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* of the matrix $X$ having *eigenvalue* $-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci yang menjadikan ini berfungsi ialah $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"Dalam istilah matematik, vektor $\\vert - \\rangle$ adalah *vektor eigen* bagi matriks $X$ yang mempunyai *nilai eigen* $-1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll discuss eigenvectors and eigenvalues in greater detail in the upcoming lesson on *Phase estimation and factoring,* where the phase kickback phenomenon is generalized to other unitary operations.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan membincangkan vektor eigen dan nilai eigen dengan lebih terperinci dalam pelajaran akan datang tentang *Anggaran fasa dan pemfaktoran,* di mana fenomena tendangan fasa digeneralisasikan kepada operasi uniter lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeping in mind that scalars float freely through tensor products, we find an alternative way of reasoning how the operation $U_f$ transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ in the analysis above:\n"
msgstr "Dengan mengingat bahawa skalar bergerak bebas melalui hasil tensor, kita menemui cara alternatif untuk memikirkan bagaimana operasi $U_f$ mengubah $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ kepada $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ dalam analisis di atas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation in Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan dalam Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how we can implement Deutsch's algorithm in Qiskit. We'll start with a version check and then perform the imports required solely for this implementation.\n"
"For the implementations of other algorithms that follows, we'll perform the required imports separately for the sake of greater modularity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita lihat bagaimana kita boleh melaksanakan algoritma Deutsch dalam Qiskit. Kita akan bermula dengan semakan versi dan kemudian melakukan import yang diperlukan khusus untuk pelaksanaan ini.\n"
"Untuk pelaksanaan algoritma lain yang berikut, kita akan melakukan import yang diperlukan secara berasingan demi modulariti yang lebih baik.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll define a quantum circuit that implements a query gate for one of the four functions $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, or $f_4$ from one bit to one bit described previously. As we already mentioned, the implementation of query gates is not really a part of Deutsch's algorithm itself;\n"
"here we're essentially just showing one way to prepare the input, in the form of a circuit implementation of a query gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama kita akan mendefinisikan litar kuantum yang melaksanakan gerbang pertanyaan untuk salah satu daripada empat fungsi $f_1,$ $f_2,$ $f_3,$ atau $f_4$ dari satu bit ke satu bit yang diterangkan sebelumnya. Seperti yang telah kita sebutkan, pelaksanaan gerbang pertanyaan sebenarnya bukan sebahagian daripada algoritma Deutsch itu sendiri;\n"
"di sini kita pada asasnya hanya menunjukkan satu cara untuk menyediakan input, dalam bentuk pelaksanaan litar gerbang pertanyaan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see what each circuit looks like using the `draw` method. Here's the circuit for the function $f_3$.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh melihat rupa setiap litar menggunakan kaedah `draw`. Berikut adalah litar untuk fungsi $f_3$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will create the actual quantum circuit for Deutsch's algorithm, substituting the query gate with a quantum circuit implementation given as an argument. Shortly we'll plug in one of the four circuits defined by the function `deutsch_function` we defined earlier.\n"
"Barriers are included to show the visual separation between the query gate implementation and the rest of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya kita akan mencipta litar kuantum sebenar untuk algoritma Deutsch, menggantikan gerbang pertanyaan dengan pelaksanaan litar kuantum yang diberikan sebagai argumen. Tidak lama lagi kita akan memasukkan salah satu daripada empat litar yang ditakrifkan oleh fungsi `deutsch_function` yang kita takrifkan sebelumnya.\n"
"Penghalang disertakan untuk menunjukkan pemisahan visual antara pelaksanaan gerbang pertanyaan dan bahagian lain litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again we can see what the circuit looks like using the `draw` method.\n"
msgstr "Sekali lagi kita boleh melihat rupa litar menggunakan kaedah `draw`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we'll create a function that runs the circuit previously defined one time and outputs the appropriate result: \"constant\" or \"balanced.\"\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, kita akan mencipta fungsi yang menjalankan litar yang ditakrifkan sebelumnya sekali dan mengeluarkan hasil yang sesuai: \"malar\" atau \"seimbang.\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run Deutsch's algorithm on any one of the four functions defined above.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini boleh menjalankan algoritma Deutsch pada mana-mana satu daripada empat fungsi yang ditakrifkan di atas.\n"
